  "notes": "Big-room house's defining producer, whose 2012 breakthrough is documented as the track that \"further popularized the big room house genre\". His entry is one of the best-equipped in this section — reFX Nexus 2 and Sylenth1 named as his favourite plug-ins with a published Sylenth1 soundset, a Roland A-49 controller, Crane Song Avocet monitoring, an SSL XLogic G-Series compressor and a Jan Morel studio from January 2015 — but gear names no generator parameter, so what is authored is the documented drop method: \"building tension through progressive breakdowns before an explosive synth-driven release\", and the arrangement he is documented as using, \"build-up, break, build-up, drop\". That is two prechorus sections in every structure, a wide authored roll ramp, and the big-room minimum of drop percussion: \"often only a kick or tom and a couple of hi-hats\", so the perc bed is 0-2 hits with a crash rather than a hand-percussion lane. The kick is \"tuned and pre-pitched with a sub layer\", so kick and bass function as one instrument at 0.96 roots. Melodies stay \"simple and minimal\" per the big-room convention. ⚠ The tempo comes from the big-room convention by the entry's own statement, and every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
